    "narrative": "With the league entering a critical stretch, our optimization strategy for today remains tethered to the scarcity of stolen bases. **Brice Turang** earns the nod at 2B today with a 47.07 efficiency score. While his matchup against Nick Pivetta presents a stiff challenge given the pitcher's 3.17 xERA, **Brice Turang** maintains relevance through his high-leverage spot in the lineup and his profile as a speed-first asset. While the base projection for **Brice Turang** was dampened by Pivetta\u2019s skill level, the dynamic platoon advantage against the right-hander provides enough upside to keep him above our floor, particularly as we hunt for stolen base efficiency in a thin daily market.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the team today involved **Dalton Rushing**, who ultimately landed on the bench with a 33.57 score. He was the primary candidate for the final slot, but he fell victim to a brutal combination of factors: an elite opposing matchup against Chris Sale (2.79 xERA) and an projected spot at the bottom of the order. The left-on-left platoon disadvantage further suppressed his expected output, signaling that **Dalton Rushing** represents a clear \"below floor\" option today. We are effectively preserving game caps by sitting him, especially as we await updates on **Corbin Carroll**, **Jose Caballero**, and **Josh Naylor**, who are all idle today. Other core assets like **James Wood**, **Mickey Moniak**, **Trevor Story**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Max Muncy**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Moises Ballesteros**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Griffin Conine**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Cole Young** remain on high alert for future slates as we monitor the volatility of our bench depth against incoming pitching projections.",
